Subject: d3d12: serialize offline descriptor frees with allocations, opt-in

With a threaded context (GALLIUM_THREAD defaults on, and st/mesa asks
for one), u_threaded_context calls create_sampler_view and
create_sampler_state directly on the frontend thread, while sampler view
releases, set_sampler_views and batch resets run on the driver thread.

d3d12_create_sampler_view allocates from the screen's view pool under
descriptor_pool_mutex, but d3d12_destroy_sampler_view frees from the same
pool without it, and the per-context sampler pool is allocated in
create_sampler_state and freed from the batch's zombie list with no lock
at all. d3d12_descriptor_handle_free and d3d12_descriptor_heap_alloc_handle
both modify the heap's `next` offset and free list, so a free racing an
allocation can hand one CPU descriptor slot to two live views. The view
created second then overwrites the first view's SRV, and every later draw
that binds the first view samples the wrong texture. The surface pools
already take the mutex on both sides (d3d12_surface.cpp). Upstream main
has the same unlocked free.

- D3D12_DESCRIPTOR_POOL_LOCK=1 takes descriptor_pool_mutex around the
  view-pool free in d3d12_destroy_sampler_view, around the sampler-pool
  allocations in d3d12_create_sampler_state, and around the zombie
  sampler frees in d3d12_reset_batch. Without it the driver behaves as
  before, so one build serves both arms of an A/B.
- D3D12_DESCRIPTOR_STATS=<path> tracks the owning thread of every offline
  descriptor slot and appends, at most once a second from
  d3d12_end_batch, the allocation and free counts, allocations of a slot
  that is still live (dup_allocs), frees of a free slot (double_frees),
  calls that found another thread inside the same heap (overlaps), frees
  on a thread other than the allocating one (cross_thread_frees), whether
  the context is threaded, and the UTC FILETIME of the first duplicate,
  double free and overlap.

